Fix shared popover collapse and left-side bookmark-bar push

- Persisted the Other windows popover display state (icons-only/collapsed versus full tabs) as winPopIcons in shared extension storage. Newly opened tabs/windows load this state, and already-open tabs/windows synchronize changes via storage.onChanged.
- Corrected horizontal bookmark-bar geometry: when the popover is left-aligned, the bar and its items now start after the popover and use the remaining width. When it is right-aligned, the bar keeps its left edge and yields width at the right. This avoids applying a right-side inset to the left-aligned case.
- Kept the separate per-window section collapse keys intact; they are not used as a substitute for the popover-wide collapsed/expanded state.

Validation: content.js and fn-bookmarks.js pass JavaScript syntax parsing. Source checks confirm persistence on load/change and side-aware bookmark-bar offset/width calculations. No live Chrome/browser UI test was run.
